              - generic:
                - paragraph: Shrinks the capacity of the vector as much as possible.
                - paragraph:
                  - text: The behavior of this method depends on the allocator, which may either shrink the vector in-place or reallocate. The resulting vector might still have some excess capacity, just as is the case for
                  - link [ref=f84e1712]:
                    - code: with_capacity
                  - text: . See
                  - link [ref=f84e1714]:
                    - /url: ../alloc/trait.Allocator.html#method.shrink
                    - code: Allocator::shrink
                  - text: for more details.
                - heading "Examples" [level=5] [ref=f84e1716]
                - code: let mut vec = Vec::with_capacity(10); vec.extend([1, 2, 3]); assert!(vec.capacity() >= 10); vec.shrink_to_fit(); assert!(vec.capacity() >= 3);
            - group:
