                  - text: method can emulate
                  - code: truncate
                  - text: ", but causes the excess elements to be returned instead of dropped."
                - paragraph: Note that this method has no effect on the allocated capacity of the vector.
                - heading "Examples" [level=5] [ref=f84e1867]
                - paragraph: "Truncating a five element vector to two elements:"
                - code: let mut vec = vec![1, 2, 3, 4, 5]; vec.truncate(2); assert_eq!(vec, [1, 2]);
                - paragraph:
                  - text: No truncation occurs when
                  - code: len
                  - text: "is greater than the vector’s current length:"
                - code: let mut vec = vec![1, 2, 3]; vec.truncate(8); assert_eq!(vec, [1, 2, 3]);
                - paragraph:
                  - text: Truncating when
                  - code: len == 0
                  - text: is equivalent to calling the
                  - link [ref=f84e1879]:
                    - /url: struct.Vec.html#method.clear
                    - code: clear
                  - text: method.
                - code: let mut vec = vec![1, 2, 3]; vec.truncate(0); assert_eq!(vec, []);
