                    - link "SliceIndex" [ref=f84e3338]
                    - text: <
                    - link "[T]" [ref=f84e3339]
                    - text: ">,"
              - text: Collapse
            - generic:
              - paragraph: Returns a reference to an element or subslice depending on the type of index.
              - list:
                - listitem:
                  - text: If given a position, returns a reference to the element at that position or
                  - code: None
                  - text: if out of bounds.
                - listitem:
                  - text: If given a range, returns the subslice corresponding to that range, or
                  - code: None
                  - text: if out of bounds.
              - heading "Examples" [level=5] [ref=f84e3347]
              - code: let v = [10, 40, 30]; assert_eq!(Some(&40), v.get(1)); assert_eq!(Some(&[10, 40][..]), v.get(0..2)); assert_eq!(None, v.get(3)); assert_eq!(None, v.get(0..4));
          - group:
            - generic:
              - generic:
                - generic:
                  - text: 1.0.0 ·
                  - link "Source" [ref=f84e3355]: ../../src/core/slice/mod.rs.html#600-602
                - heading [level=4] [ref=f84e3356]:
                  - text: pub fn
                  - link "get_mut" [ref=f84e3357]
                  - text: "<I>( &mut self, index: I, ) ->"
                  - link "Option" [ref=f84e3358]
                  - text: <&mut <I as
                  - link "SliceIndex" [ref=f84e3359]
                  - text: <
                  - link "[T]" [ref=f84e3360]
                  - text: ">>::"
                  - link "Output" [ref=f84e3361]
                  - text: ">"
                  - generic:
                    - text: "where I:"
                    - link "SliceIndex" [ref=f84e3363]
                    - text: <
                    - link "[T]" [ref=f84e3364]
                    - text: ">,"
              - text: Collapse
            - generic:
              - paragraph:
                - text: Returns a mutable reference to an element or subslice depending on the type of index (see
                - link [ref=f84e3367]:
                  - code: get
                - text: ) or
                - code: None
                - text: if the index is out of bounds.
              - heading "Examples" [level=5] [ref=f84e3370]
              - code: "let x = &mut [0, 1, 2]; if let Some(elem) = x.get_mut(1) { *elem = 42; } assert_eq!(x, &[0, 42, 2]);"
          - group:
            - generic:
              - generic:
                - generic:
                  - text: 1.0.0 ·
                  - link "Source" [ref=f84e3378]: ../../src/core/slice/mod.rs.html#640-642
                - heading [level=4] [ref=f84e3379]:
                  - text: pub unsafe fn
                  - link "get_unchecked" [ref=f84e3380]
                  - text: "<I>( &self, index: I, ) -> &<I as"
                  - link "SliceIndex" [ref=f84e3381]
                  - text: <
                  - link "[T]" [ref=f84e3382]
                  - text: ">>::"
                  - link "Output" [ref=f84e3383]
                  - generic:
                    - text: "where I:"
                    - link "SliceIndex" [ref=f84e3385]
                    - text: <
                    - link "[T]" [ref=f84e3386]
                    - text: ">,"
              - text: Collapse
            - generic:
              - paragraph: Returns a reference to an element or subslice, without doing bounds checking.
              - paragraph:
                - text: For a safe alternative see
                - link [ref=f84e3390]:
                  - code: get
                - text: .
              - heading "Safety" [level=5] [ref=f84e3392]
              - paragraph:
                - text: Calling this method with an out-of-bounds index is
                - emphasis:
                  - link "undefined behavior" [ref=f84e3395]: https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/behavior-considered-undefined.html
                - text: even if the resulting reference is not used.
              - paragraph:
                - text: You can think of this like
                - code: .get(index).unwrap_unchecked()
                - text: . It’s UB to call
                - code: .get_unchecked(len)
                - text: ", even if you immediately convert to a pointer. And it’s UB to call"
                - code: .get_unchecked(..len + 1)
                - code: .get_unchecked(..=len)
                - text: ", or similar."
              - heading "Examples" [level=5] [ref=f84e3401]
              - code: "let x = &[1, 2, 4]; unsafe { assert_eq!(x.get_unchecked(1), &2); }"
          - group:
            - generic:
              - generic:
                - generic:
                  - text: 1.0.0 ·
                  - link "Source" [ref=f84e3409]: ../../src/core/slice/mod.rs.html#686-688
                - heading [level=4] [ref=f84e3410]:
                  - text: pub unsafe fn
                  - link "get_unchecked_mut" [ref=f84e3411]
                  - text: "<I>( &mut self, index: I, ) -> &mut <I as"
                  - link "SliceIndex" [ref=f84e3412]
                  - text: <
