              - text: Collapse
            - generic:
              - paragraph: Returns a raw pointer to the slice’s buffer.
              - paragraph: The caller must ensure that the slice outlives the pointer this function returns, or else it will end up dangling.
              - paragraph:
                - text: The caller must also ensure that the memory the pointer (non-transitively) points to is never written to (except inside an
                - code: UnsafeCell
                - text: ) using this pointer or any pointer derived from it. If you need to mutate the contents of the slice, use
                - link [ref=f84e3449]:
                  - /url: ../primitive.slice.html#method.as_mut_ptr
                  - code: as_mut_ptr
                - text: .
              - paragraph: Modifying the container referenced by this slice may cause its buffer to be reallocated, which would also make any pointers to it invalid.
              - heading "Examples" [level=5] [ref=f84e3452]
              - code: "let x = &[1, 2, 4]; let x_ptr = x.as_ptr(); unsafe { for i in 0..x.len() { assert_eq!(x.get_unchecked(i), &*x_ptr.add(i)); } }"
          - group:
