            - generic:
              - paragraph: Returns the two raw pointers spanning the slice.
              - paragraph:
                - text: The returned range is half-open, which means that the end pointer points
                - emphasis: one past
                - text: the last element of the slice. This way, an empty slice is represented by two equal pointers, and the difference between the two pointers represents the size of the slice.
              - paragraph:
                - text: See
                - link [ref=f84e3487]:
                  - /url: ../primitive.slice.html#method.as_ptr
                  - code: as_ptr
                - text: for warnings on using these pointers. The end pointer requires extra caution, as it does not point to a valid element in the slice.
              - paragraph: This function is useful for interacting with foreign interfaces which use two pointers to refer to a range of elements in memory, as is common in C++.
              - paragraph: "It can also be useful to check if a pointer to an element refers to an element of this slice:"
              - code: let a = [1, 2, 3]; let x = &a[1] as *const _; let y = &5 as *const _; assert!(a.as_ptr_range().contains(&x)); assert!(!a.as_ptr_range().contains(&y));
