                  - text: )
              - text: Collapse
            - generic:
              - paragraph: Divides one slice into two at an index.
              - paragraph:
                - text: The first will contain all indices from
                - code: "[0, mid)"
                - text: (excluding the index
                - code: mid
                - text: itself) and the second will contain all indices from
                - code: "[mid, len)"
                - text: (excluding the index
                - code: len
                - text: itself).
              - heading "Panics" [level=5] [ref=f84e4295]
              - paragraph:
                - text: Panics if
                - code: mid > len
                - text: . For a non-panicking alternative see
                - link [ref=f84e4298]:
                  - /url: ../primitive.slice.html#method.split_at_checked
                  - code: split_at_checked
                - text: .
              - heading "Examples" [level=5] [ref=f84e4300]
              - code: "let v = ['a', 'b', 'c']; { let (left, right) = v.split_at(0); assert_eq!(left, []); assert_eq!(right, ['a', 'b', 'c']); } { let (left, right) = v.split_at(2); assert_eq!(left, ['a', 'b']); assert_eq!(right, ['c']); } { let (left, right) = v.split_at(3); assert_eq!(left, ['a', 'b', 'c']); assert_eq!(right, []); }"
