                - code: mid ≤ len
                - text: returns a pair of slices where the first will contain all indices from
                - code: "[0, mid)"
                - text: (excluding the index
                - code: mid
                - text: itself) and the second will contain all indices from
                - code: "[mid, len)"
                - text: (excluding the index
                - code: len
                - text: itself).
              - paragraph:
                - text: Otherwise, if
                - code: mid > len
                - text: ", returns"
                - code: None
                - text: .
              - heading "Examples" [level=5] [ref=f84e4411]
              - code: "let v = [1, -2, 3, -4, 5, -6]; { let (left, right) = v.split_at_checked(0).unwrap(); assert_eq!(left, []); assert_eq!(right, [1, -2, 3, -4, 5, -6]); } { let (left, right) = v.split_at_checked(2).unwrap(); assert_eq!(left, [1, -2]); assert_eq!(right, [3, -4, 5, -6]); } { let (left, right) = v.split_at_checked(6).unwrap(); assert_eq!(left, [1, -2, 3, -4, 5, -6]); assert_eq!(right, []); } assert_eq!(None, v.split_at_checked(7));"
