                  - text: )
              - text: Collapse
            - generic:
              - paragraph: Returns a subslice with the optional prefix removed.
              - paragraph:
                - text: If the slice starts with
                - code: prefix
                - text: ", returns the subslice after the prefix. If"
                - code: prefix
                - text: is empty or the slice does not start with
                - code: prefix
                - text: ", simply returns the original slice. If"
                - code: prefix
                - text: is equal to the original slice, returns an empty slice.
              - heading "Examples" [level=5] [ref=f84e4922]
              - code: "#![feature(trim_prefix_suffix)] let v = &[10, 40, 30]; // Prefix present - removes it assert_eq!(v.trim_prefix(&[10]), &[40, 30][..]); assert_eq!(v.trim_prefix(&[10, 40]), &[30][..]); assert_eq!(v.trim_prefix(&[10, 40, 30]), &[][..]); // Prefix absent - returns original slice assert_eq!(v.trim_prefix(&[50]), &[10, 40, 30][..]); assert_eq!(v.trim_prefix(&[10, 50]), &[10, 40, 30][..]); let prefix : &str = \"he\"; assert_eq!(b\"hello\".trim_prefix(prefix.as_bytes()), b\"llo\".as_ref());"
          - group:
