                - link "total order" [ref=f84e5214]
                - text: ", the function may panic; even if the function exits normally, the resulting order of elements in the slice is unspecified. See also the note on panicking below."
              - paragraph:
                - text: For example
                - code: "|a, b| (a - b).cmp(a)"
                - text: is a comparison function that is neither transitive nor reflexive nor total,
                - code: a < b < c < a
                - text: with
                - code: a = 1, b = 2, c = 3
                - text: . For more information and examples see the
                - link [ref=f84e5219]:
                  - code: Ord
                - text: documentation.
              - paragraph:
                - text: All original elements will remain in the slice and any possible modifications via interior mutability are observed in the input. Same is true if the implementation of
                - link [ref=f84e5222]:
                  - code: Ord
                - text: for
                - code: K
                - text: panics.
              - heading "Current implementation" [level=5] [ref=f84e5225]
              - paragraph:
                - text: The current implementation is based on
                - link "ipnsort" [ref=f84e5227]
                - text: by Lukas Bergdoll and Orson Peters, which combines the fast average case of quicksort with the fast worst case of heapsort, achieving linear time on fully sorted and reversed inputs. On inputs with k distinct elements, the expected time to sort the data is
                - emphasis: O
                - text: (
                - emphasis: "n"
                - text: "* log("
                - emphasis: k
                - text: )).
              - paragraph: It is typically faster than stable sorting, except in a few special cases, e.g., when the slice is partially sorted.
              - heading "Panics" [level=5] [ref=f84e5232]
              - paragraph:
                - text: May panic if the implementation of
                - link [ref=f84e5234]:
                  - code: Ord
                - text: for
                - code: K
                - text: does not implement a
                - link "total order" [ref=f84e5237]
                - text: ", or if the"
                - link [ref=f84e5238]:
                  - code: Ord
                - text: implementation panics.
              - heading "Examples" [level=5] [ref=f84e5240]
              - code: let mut v = [4i32, -5, 1, -3, 2]; v.sort_unstable_by_key(|k| k.abs()); assert_eq!(v, [1, 2, -3, 4, -5]);
          - group:
            - generic:
              - generic:
                - link "Source" [ref=f84e5247]: ../../src/core/slice/mod.rs.html#3325-3328
                - heading [level=4] [ref=f84e5248]:
                  - text: pub fn
                  - link "partial_sort_unstable" [ref=f84e5249]
                  - text: "<R>(&mut self, range: R)"
                  - generic:
                    - text: "where T:"
                    - link "Ord" [ref=f84e5251]
                    - text: ", R:"
