              - paragraph: "Swapping two elements across slices:"
              - code: let mut slice1 = [0, 0]; let mut slice2 = [1, 2, 3, 4]; slice1.swap_with_slice(&mut slice2[2..]); assert_eq!(slice1, [3, 4]); assert_eq!(slice2, [1, 2, 0, 0]);
              - paragraph:
                - text: Rust enforces that there can only be one mutable reference to a particular piece of data in a particular scope. Because of this, attempting to use
                - code: swap_with_slice
                - text: "on a single slice will result in a compile failure:"
              - generic:
