              - paragraph: "This method splits the slice into three distinct slices: prefix, correctly aligned middle slice of a new type, and the suffix slice. The middle part will be as big as possible under the given alignment constraint and element size."
              - paragraph:
                - text: This method has no purpose when either input element
                - code: T
                - text: or output element
                - code: U
                - text: are zero-sized and will return the original slice without splitting anything.
              - heading "Safety" [level=5] [ref=f84e5967]
              - paragraph:
                - text: This method is essentially a
                - code: transmute
                - text: with respect to the elements in the returned middle slice, so all the usual caveats pertaining to
                - code: transmute::<T, U>
                - text: also apply here.
              - heading "Examples" [level=5] [ref=f84e5971]
              - paragraph: "Basic usage:"
              - code: "unsafe { let bytes: [u8; 7] = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7]; let (prefix, shorts, suffix) = bytes.align_to::<u16>(); // less_efficient_algorithm_for_bytes(prefix); // more_efficient_algorithm_for_aligned_shorts(shorts); // less_efficient_algorithm_for_bytes(suffix); }"
