            - generic:
              - paragraph: Returns the index that an element reference points to.
              - paragraph:
                - text: Returns
                - code: None
                - text: if
                - code: element
                - text: does not point to the start of an element within the slice.
              - paragraph:
                - text: This method is useful for extending slice iterators like
                - link [ref=f84e6408]:
                  - /url: ../primitive.slice.html#method.split
                  - code: slice::split
                - text: .
              - paragraph:
                - text: Note that this uses pointer arithmetic and
                - strong: does not compare elements
                - text: . To find the index of an element via comparison, use
                - link [ref=f84e6412]:
                  - /url: ../iter/trait.Iterator.html#method.position
                  - code: .iter().position()
                - text: instead.
              - heading "Panics" [level=5] [ref=f84e6414]
              - paragraph:
                - text: Panics if
                - code: T
                - text: is zero-sized.
              - heading "Examples" [level=5] [ref=f84e6417]
              - paragraph: "Basic usage:"
              - code: "let nums: &[u32] = &[1, 7, 1, 1]; let num = &nums[2]; assert_eq!(num, &1); assert_eq!(nums.element_offset(num), Some(2));"
              - paragraph:
                - text: Returning
                - code: None
                - text: "with an unaligned element:"
              - code: "let arr: &[[u32; 2]] = &[[0, 1], [2, 3]]; let flat_arr: &[u32] = arr.as_flattened(); let ok_elm: &[u32; 2] = flat_arr[0..2].try_into().unwrap(); let weird_elm: &[u32; 2] = flat_arr[1..3].try_into().unwrap(); assert_eq!(ok_elm, &[0, 1]); assert_eq!(weird_elm, &[1, 2]); assert_eq!(arr.element_offset(ok_elm), Some(0)); // Points to element 0 assert_eq!(arr.element_offset(weird_elm), None); // Points between element 0 and 1"
          - group:
