                  - link "Cow" [ref=f84e7595]
                  - text: <'a,
                  - link "[T]" [ref=f84e7596]
                  - text: ">) ->"
                  - link "Vec" [ref=f84e7597]
                  - text: <T>
              - text: Collapse
            - generic:
              - paragraph: Converts a clone-on-write slice into a vector.
              - paragraph:
                - text: If
                - code: s
                - text: already owns a
                - code: Vec<T>
                - text: ", it will be returned directly. If"
                - code: s
                - text: is borrowing a slice, a new
                - code: Vec<T>
                - text: will be allocated and filled by cloning
                - code: s
                - text: ’s items into it.
              - heading "Examples" [level=5] [ref=f84e7606]
              - code: "let o: Cow<'_, [i32]> = Cow::Owned(vec![1, 2, 3]); let b: Cow<'_, [i32]> = Cow::Borrowed(&[1, 2, 3]); assert_eq!(Vec::from(o), Vec::from(b));"
        - group:
